---
export const title = 'Variants, sizes and states';
export const order = 400;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  The cells sit in one field box, so pin input takes the same <code>variant</code>,
  <code>size</code> (<code>sm</code> by default), helper, error and warning options as the other
  fields. Set <code>--pin-input-cell-width</code> to change the width of the cells.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-pin-input label='Filled' variant='filled' value='123'></wc-pin-input>
    <wc-pin-input label='Medium' size='md' value='123'></wc-pin-input>
    <wc-pin-input label='Error' error error-text='That code is not right' value='123456'></wc-pin-input>
    <wc-pin-input label='Disabled' disabled value='123456'></wc-pin-input>
    <wc-pin-input label='Read only' readonly value='123456'></wc-pin-input>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Forms and validation</h3>
<p>
  Inside a <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> the code is submitted under its <code>name</code>, and
  <code>form.reset()</code> restores its first value. With <code>required</code>, an empty code is
  <code>valueMissing</code>. A code that is started but not complete is <code>tooShort</code>,
  whether required or not, like text under a native <code>minlength</code>. The message shows under
  the cells once the code is committed or the form is submitted.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <form id='pin-input-form' style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start;'>
    <wc-pin-input name='code' label='Verification code' required></wc-pin-input>
    <wc-button type='submit'>Verify</wc-button>
  </form>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#pin-input-form').addEventListener('submit', function (event) {
      event.preventDefault();
      myConsole.log('code: ' + new FormData(event.target).get('code'));
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>
<p>
  The cells form a group named by <code>label</code>; each cell is named by its position, such as
  "Digit 2 of 6" (the <code>pinInputDigit</code> and <code>pinInputCharacter</code> strings). The
  helper or error text is linked to every cell with <code>aria-describedby</code>.
</p>
